== 1. A two-cluster Kubara platform: hub in dev, spoke in prod, as in kubara-confighub's kind lab
$ cub kubara init --out platform --hub hub:dev --spoke spoke:prod --services cert-manager,metrics-server,traefik,homer-dashboard --repository http://git.git-server.svc.cluster.local/platform.git --email lab@example.com
wrote platform/config.yaml
wrote platform/.env.example
wrote platform/confighub-intent.yaml
left out homer-dashboard on spoke (a spoke; it runs only on hub)

Next
  cp platform/.env.example platform/.env   # then fill in the values it asks for
  kubara --work-dir platform --config-file config.yaml --env-file .env generate --helm
  cub kubara plan platform
$ kubara --work-dir . --config-file config.yaml --env-file .env generate --helm
2026-09-30 17:57:03 INF All files generated successfully.
✅ Templating complete! Don't forget to PUSH the changes to apply them!
$ ls platform-components/helm
argo-cd
bootstrap-crds
cert-manager
homer-dashboard
metrics-server
template-library
traefik

